\pard\sb200\sa120\b\fs22 6. Data and network connections\b0\fs20\par
\pard\sa120\fs20 Vadgr stores its settings, credentials, paired-device information and task history on your computer. This version does not require a Publisher-operated cloud service and does not send product telemetry to the Publisher.\par
\pard\sa120\fs20 Data leaves your computer when a feature requires it. Prompts and relevant task context go to the model provider you selected. Tool requests go to the tools and services you connected. Paired-device traffic uses the connection method you selected.\par
\pard\sa120\fs20 The built-in connection first tries a direct encrypted path. It can use a relay when a direct path is unavailable. A relay cannot read the end-to-end encrypted Vadgr content. It can observe connection information, including network addresses, endpoint public keys, connection times and traffic volume. If you select Tailscale, your Tailscale configuration and Tailscale's terms apply.\par
\pard\sa120\fs20 An update check or download contacts the update source configured in this copy or the source you select. That source can observe normal request information, including your network address and the request time. Normal use, local settings, offline repair and uninstall do not require access to a source-code repository.\par
\pard\sb200\sa120\b\fs22 7. Security and availability\b0\fs20\par
\pard\sa120\fs20 No security control removes all risks from computer control. A person or process with access to your computer, credentials, pairing information or providers can act with the authority those items give. Use the narrowest permissions that work. Revoke a lost device or credential. Keep your operating system and Vadgr updated. Keep backups outside Vadgr.\par
